# Let the telemetry service set ONLY the system timezone and (re)enable NTP —
# never set the clock directly. The dashboard pushes the unit's GPS-derived
# timezone in the heartbeat and the device applies it so its local-time WittyPi
# wake window is correct; `set-ntp true` is the idempotent nudge telemetry uses
# when a beat lands but the clock isn't disciplined yet (the RTC is then written
# only AFTER NTP reports synchronized). timedatectl validates its own inputs and
# can't strand the unit. Installed by hardware/provision.sh.
beemonitor ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/timedatectl set-timezone *
beemonitor ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/timedatectl set-ntp *
